Rhombus/HOL third-party scope index
===================================

Document roles
--------------

LICENSE contains only the 0BSD terms for original Rhombus/HOL material.
This file maps repository components to third-party notices.
LICENSES/ contains the complete retained notices and license terms.

Component notices
-----------------

- rhombus-hol-kernel/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES maps the executable kernel to
  HOL Light.
- rhombus-hol-lib/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES maps the derived library to HOL Light,
  HOL4, ACL2, and QuickCheck.
- rhombus-hol/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES maps generated documentation assets to
  Scribble/Racket and the embedded fonts.
- isabelle-hol-kernel/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES maps the formalization and generated
  proof presentation to HOL Light, HOL4, and Isabelle.

Each independently distributable package repeats only the applicable files
from LICENSES/ so its source archive remains self-contained. The package-local
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES file is the authoritative scope map for that package.

Conservative treatment
----------------------

This repository was developed with coding agents and contains implementations
that closely follow established theorem-prover designs. The scope maps retain
upstream notices without relying on a narrow distinction between copyrightable
source expression and uncopyrighted ideas or interfaces. This does not assert
that every mapped file contains copyrightable material from every named
project.

The GitHub Pages artifact also includes this index and all files from LICENSES/.
